question:
Deck Management (Deck Management)
Are procedures in place to carry out regular inspections of fuel and ballast tanks, void spaces, trunks and cofferdams by the vessel’s personnel and are records maintained?
A. Fuel tanks to be inspected atleast one every dry dock;
B. Ballast tanks shall be internally inspected at least every 12 months to check sedimentation or deterioration of coating and wastage of anodes, if fitted;
C. Hold spaces, Void spaces, cofferdams shall be internally inspected atleast every 12 months for deterioration
